CLI-18: gmk_m2 -e -t writes a wrong arc count in the header for tori with both dimensions < 3 (src/scotch/gmk_m2.c).
Run:  B=$TREE/bin; export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$TREE/lib
  for d0 in 1 2 3 4; do for d1 in 1 2 3 4; do $B/gmk_m2 $d0 $d1 -e -t g.grf; hdr=$(sed -n 2p g.grf | cut -f2); \
    cnt=$(tail -n +4 g.grf | awk '{s+=$1} END{print s+0}'); $B/gtst g.grf >/dev/null 2>&1; echo "$d0x$d1 header=$hdr written=$cnt gtst_rc=$?"; done; done
Pristine: 1x1 header=-4 written=0, 1x2 -2/2, 2x1 -2/2, 2x2 8/12: all four fail to load (gtst rc=1); other sizes OK; plain -t OK.
Patched: header == written for all 16 sizes, gtst rc=0 everywhere.
Byte-compare with pristine 7.0.17 gmk_m2 over d0,d1 in 1..5 x {"", -e, -t, "-e -t", "-b1 -e -t", "-b1 -t"} (150 files):
  142 identical, the 8 that differ are exactly the "-e -t"/"-b1 -e -t" files with d0,d1 <= 2 (header line only).
  Generators sweep (gmk_m2 all flags, gmk_m3 +-t, mmk_m2, mmk_m3, gmk_hy, gmk_ub2 at dims 1..3): only those 4 gmk_m2 cases fail.
Regression tests added: check_prog_gmk (+ CMake): gmk_m2 -e -t 2 2 / 1 2 / 2 1 / 1 1 | gtst.
